      "text_raw": "The capacitances at the top\nnodes 5, 6 and 7 also cause\nnon-dominant poles. They\nare followed by zeros how-\never, at double the fre-\nquency. Indeed, each time\nwe have a single-ended\namplifier, the capacitances\non the other side than the\noutput, will be negligible for\nthe Phase Margin.\nAs a conclusion, this OTA\nhas only one single non-\ndominant pole. It is fairly\neasy to design. It also has\nthe advantage that it is\nvery fast.",
      "text": "The capacitances at the top nodes 5, 6 and 7 also cause non-dominant poles. They are followed by zeros however, at double the frequency. Indeed, each time we have a single-ended amplifier, the capacitances on the other side than the output, will be negligible for the Phase Margin. As a conclusion, this OTA has only one single nondominant pole. It is fairly easy to design. It also has the advantage that it is very fast."
